cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Temporal Equivalence Principle: Synchronization Holonomy in Pulsar Scintillation"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Smawfield"
    given-names: "Matthew Lukin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8219-3159"
abstract: >
  Standard scintillation models predict zero phase closure around delay triplets. TEP predicts path-dependent proper-time transport (synchronization holonomy) in low-density sightlines. PSR J0437-4715 shows weighted phase closure psi = 0.984 ± 0.046 rad (Rayleigh p = 1.34 × 10^-44), rejecting the scalar-delay null; multi-pulsar checks are directionally consistent with TEP environmental screening.
